// Trails write surface (RFD-023 trails-native port, PR 2 Task 5): validation,
// create/update/delete handlers, and their response serializers. Ported from
// the trails-service spike's src/trail-create.ts, src/trail-update.ts,
// src/trail-delete.ts, src/branch-name.ts, src/trail-assignees.ts, and the
// relevant slice of src/app.ts (the POST/PATCH/DELETE handlers) — see those
// files (git show spike/trails-stack-8-devex:spikes/trails-service/src/...)
// for the authoritative behavioral spec this file mirrors.
//
// Every optional JSON body field is bound as json.RawMessage (present ⟺
// len>0) rather than a plain Go-typed field: the spike's validation funcs
// distinguish "key absent" (undefined) from "key present" at several points
// (independent of the JS `undefined`-vs-`null` distinction, which this port
// deliberately collapses — see rawAsString/rawAsStringSlice), and a plain
// typed field (e.g. []string for assignees) would let Huma's schema-based
// body binding reject a malformed value (e.g. a non-string element) before
// our handler-level validation ever runs, producing Huma's own error message
// instead of the spike's exact "assignees must be an array of strings".
// json.RawMessage sidesteps that: Huma decodes it as opaque bytes, and this
// file's own decode helpers reproduce the spike's runtime typeof/Array.isArray
// checks by hand.

