// Editor-document sync surface (ENT-1231): the rehydrate (GET) read API for
// the trail-body editor Durable Object on the entire.io edge. The surface is
// read-only; the merge endpoint (editor_updates.go) is the only writer — see
// its file header for why every write merges and none overwrite.
//
// Auth: the caller is the trails service account (the DO federates through
// CF Access → core STS, the same chain as the ingest dual-write) presenting an
// ordinary jurisdiction token, so the route gates on the same seam as every
// other authenticated route: requireAuth verifies the token, then
// requireEditorSyncAccess authorizes the caller for sync_editor_documents on
// the platform object in live SpiceDB. End-user authorization happens at the
// BFF ws route before a socket ever reaches the DO.

